rong for silver. New Zealand’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/49640"} "Anthony Mosse"] " had been second to Groß at 150, but fell back slightly, stilling winning a bronze medal. This was the final individual Olympic event for " [:a {:href "/athletes/47812"} "Michael Groß"] ". He ended his Olympic career with six medals and three Olympic gold medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "204"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47812"} "Michael Groß"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRG.png"}] "FRG"]] [:td {} "1:58.09 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:56.94 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "130"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46335"} "Benny Nielsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} "1:59.26 (2 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:58.24 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "436"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/49640"} "Anthony Mosse"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "1:58.71 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:58.28 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "85"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46008"} "Tom Ponting"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [